Add keyboard type, secure entry and autofill hint to TextInputConfiguration.

What: three fields on `TextInputConfiguration`:
- `keyboard_type: KeyboardType`: Text, Number, Decimal, Phone, Email, Url or Search (the HTML `inputmode` set).
  The default is Text.
- `secure: bool`: password entry.
- `autofill: Option<AutofillHint>`: Username, Password, NewPassword, OneTimeCode, Email, Phone, Name, PostalAddress,
  PostalCode or CreditCardNumber.
This is data only: no backend reads the fields yet. The iOS test that builds the struct as a literal gains
`..Default::default()`.

Why: software keyboards need the right layout (digits for a PIN, `@` for email). Password fields must be hidden and
kept out of suggestions. Platform autofill needs to know what a field holds. Upstream's configuration covers only
autocorrect, autocapitalize, suggestions and the action key.

Test: `text_input_configuration_and_focus_state_are_forwarded_on_change` (input.rs) also forwards the new fields.

Upstream PR: not filed yet.

